From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Retire the native VI render mode outside the device lock
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Native VI shutdown reset its device state and then retired the render mode
while still holding the VI device mutex. Leaving the 640x448 source mode
prepares an EFB resize, which submits the active native GX hardware frame and
joins the render worker. Once that join waits longer than its 1 ms pump
interval it services owner interrupts, and the VI service locks the same
non-recursive mutex. The owner deadlocks, stops pumping window events and the
window stops responding.

Without an owner-side GPU wait after every desktop present, the final GX frame
can wait behind queued presentation work at shutdown, so the bounded original
Credits resize checks reached this path.

Commit the retired state under the lock, then retire the render mode after
releasing it. The interrupt service now sees the uninitialized device and
returns without delivering anything. Shutdown order, device callbacks and the
render-mode reset are unchanged.

diff --git a/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp b/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
index 94dd0de..76aeae7 100644
--- a/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
@@ -346,13 +346,18 @@ void aurora_shutdown_video_hardware() {
   struct Active { Device& state; ~Active() { std::lock_guard lock(state.mutex); state.active = false; } } active{state};
   if (output_attached) output.shutdown(output.context);
   if (attached) device.shutdown(device.context);
-  std::lock_guard lock(state.mutex);
-  state.initialized = state.configured = state.interrupt = state.flush = false;
-  state.interrupt_device_attached = false; state.interrupt_device = {};
-  state.output_attached = false; state.output_device = {};
-  state.config = {}; state.owner = {}; state.pre = state.post = nullptr;
-  state.dimming_request = VI_DM_DEFAULT; state.pending_dimming_threshold = state.dimming_tv_format = 0;
-  state.current_buffer = state.next_buffer = nullptr;
+  {
+    std::lock_guard lock(state.mutex);
+    state.initialized = state.configured = state.interrupt = state.flush = false;
+    state.interrupt_device_attached = false; state.interrupt_device = {};
+    state.output_attached = false; state.output_device = {};
+    state.config = {}; state.owner = {}; state.pre = state.post = nullptr;
+    state.dimming_request = VI_DM_DEFAULT; state.pending_dimming_threshold = state.dimming_tv_format = 0;
+    state.current_buffer = state.next_buffer = nullptr;
+  }
+  // Retiring the render mode can join submitted GX work, and that wait services
+  // owner interrupts. Release the non-recursive device lock first; the service
+  // then observes the retired device instead of blocking on this lock.
   aurora::vi::configure(nullptr);
 }
 bool aurora_get_video_hardware_state(AuroraVIHardwareState* result) {
